                <fr:title text="Real-Time Proving and the zkEVM Target">Real-Time Proving and the zkEVM Target</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    What the protocol actually asks of a prover, stated as numbers, and which part of the <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003R/" title="The zkVM Stack" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003R/" display-uri="dhsorens-003R" type="local">stack</fr:link> each number constrains.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>The current latency, cost, hardware, and proof-size targets, with a source for each.</html:li>
        <html:li>Proving an L1 block: what dominates — <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0048/" title="ZK-Friendly Primitives" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0048/" display-uri="dhsorens-0048" type="local">hashing</fr:link>, signature verification, state access.</html:li>
        <html:li>Verification on the consumer side: what a home verifier must be able to check, and in what time.</html:li>
        <html:li>Multi-prover and diversity arguments, and what they assume about implementation independence.</html:li>
        <html:li>Which targets are met today and which are not.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
